{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own platform record trips the anti-farming guard in POL-NS-07. EV-DPROF-00207 records driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d of 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 against driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 61 works out at 11.5 percent, which is above the 0.08 rate limb. Both limbs of the check are met on this trip's evidence, so this is the second limb of POL-NS-07 engaging, not a borderline call.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because both limbs of the anti-farming check are met, POL-NS-07 withholds the driver's compensation and routes the case to escalation under POL-NS-09, and it obliges the escalation packet to direct the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full, precisely so that the rider does not fund a dispute the platform has not resolved. EV-FARE-00207 shows the $4.00 sitting at PENDING with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so nothing has been taken from the rider and the packet instruction is that the $4.00 be returned.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207", "EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation is the correct disposition and is terminal for the automated pipeline: under POL-NS-09 no monetary ruling issues and the disputed cancellation fee is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded, and under POL-GEN-03 ESCALATE is party-relative - the disputed amount is held. On a rider-filed dispute over a fee still at PENDING, that is the outcome the rider presses for, because the $4.00 stays uncollected while the platform's own integrity question on this driver is open.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The escalation trigger is not built on degraded material. EV-DPROF-00207 is COMPLETE with an empty issues list and weight_multiplier 1.0, so there is no POL-GEN-02 discount to apply to the no-show-termination and completed-trip counters, and the escalation rests on a clean artifact rather than on an impairment of the rider's choosing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's relief here does not run through POL-NS-06, and I do not stretch it to say otherwise: the driver's own telemetry shows a single continuous qualifying in-geofence run of 507 seconds, 06:41:10 to 06:49:37, against the 300 second STANDARD minimum, so there is no waiting-period shortfall. The route to the rider not carrying this charge is the POL-NS-07 anti-farming escalation, not a dwell finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nor does the rider's case run through POL-NS-04, and I do not pretend it does. EV-CHAT-00207 holds four entries and every one is sent by the SYSTEM or the driver; the rider wrote nothing during the waiting window, so limb (a) of the rider-contact clause - a locating or coordinating message from the rider - is not met, and the rider cannot invoke that exoneration on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the driver's compensation is withheld under the anti-farming check."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case is escalated to a human reviewer. The automated pipeline issues no payment and no refund, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee stays on hold (fare_breakdown.payment_status is PENDING) — it is not collected from the rider and not returned — while the review is pending.\n\nOn the merits the trip record favours the driver. The 'arrived' marker at 06:41:20 lands on a qualifying in-geofence fix; the GPS trace places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD pick-up radius from 06:41:10 with 52 consecutive qualifying fixes; he held position continuously inside the geofence for 507 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum; and the trip was terminated by the driver at 06:49:37 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, more than three minutes after the minimum dwell elapsed at 06:46:10. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold and the $4.00 fee is chargeable on the merits. The rider's account that she came down only a few minutes late is not borne out: her device sat roughly 1.9 km from the pin for the whole window with no qualifying rider fix, and POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her because she sent no locating or coordinating message — all four chat entries are from the system or the driver. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) and POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) do not apply on these facts, and POL-NS-06 produces no shortfall, so no clause displaces POL-NS-01.\n\nThe case still cannot close with a money ruling, because the driver's own profile trips POL-NS-07's anti-farming guard: 7 no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days (the clause reads 4 or more) across 61 completed trips, a rate of 11.5% against the 8% ceiling. Both limbs are met on clean, weight-1.0 profile evidence. Where both limbs trip, POL-NS-07 withholds the driver's compensation — the $3.20 that would otherwise have been paid is not paid — and sends the case to escalation under POL-NS-09, which is terminal for the automated pipeline and holds the fee rather than collecting or refunding it. The escalation packet carries the POL-NS-07 instruction that the reviewer refund the rider's cancellation fee in full.\n\nTwo further points. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00207-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed and carries no fact; it is not needed here, because the driver's 507-second hold was one unbroken in-geofence run that requires no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i). And the fare line is sound: $4.00 is the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, so POL-NS-08(d) raises no integrity defect. This escalation is not a refund to the rider; it is a hold on the fee while the platform's open integrity question on this driver is settled."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{"type":"json_object","ruling":{"ruling":"ESCALATE","amount_sgd":null,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":["POL-NS-07 — direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the fee is held at PENDING and is neither collected nor refunded by the automated pipeline pending review."],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"To the rider: your account was tested against the platform record and the record does not place you at the pickup point. The GPS trace puts your device about 1.9 km from the pin for the whole waiting window, you sent no message, and the driver's in-app call at 06:45:10 went unanswered. On the merits the $4.00 fee was correctly chargeable. POL-NS-01 is satisfied on all four limbs: the trip record shows the driver's 'arrived' event at 06:41:20; the GPS trace places him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup zone from 06:41:10, ten seconds earlier; he held position continuously for 507 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum; and he terminated the trip at 06:49:37 on RIDER_NO_SHOW, 207 seconds after the minimum had run. POL-NS-02's arrival test is met with 52 qualifying fixes and a nearest approach of 14.5 m. The rider-side routes do not fire: the arrival marker was not false (POL-NS-05 — he was stationary inside the zone, so the corrected dwell is the full 507 s); there is no waiting shortfall (POL-NS-06 — surplus, not shortfall); there is no wrong-entrance case (POL-NS-03 — he was inside the arrival radius, not outside it); and POL-NS-04 fails at its first limb because the chat log contains no locating or coordinating message from you, only SYSTEM and DRIVER entries, and limb (c) is in any event failed on your own track. Assessed alone, that would leave the charge standing.

To the driver: that outcome does not issue here, and it is your own record that changes it. POL-NS-07 compensates you at 80% of the fee (SGD 3.20) only if its anti-farming check is clean. It is not: your profile shows 7 no-show terminations in the last 30 days against 61 completed trips, 11.5%, clearing both the count limb (4 or more) and the rate limb (above 8%). Compensation is therefore withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). You argued this yourself and the record supports it.

To both: escalation under POL-NS-09(d) is terminal for the automated pipeline. No money moves now — the $4.00 sits at PENDING, neither collected from the rider nor refunded, until a human reviewer decides. The escalation packet carries POL-NS-07's requirement that the reviewer refund the rider's cancellation fee in full. All artifacts carrying the deciding facts — EV-TRIP-00207, EV-GPS-00207 and EV-DPROF-00207 — are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so no POL-GEN-02 discount applies and confidence is not capped below 1.0. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0) and carries no fact: its absence only makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, which is immaterial because the driver's 507-second hold was a single unbroken in-geofence run. The open question for the reviewer is whether the driver's no-show termination pattern is genuine fee-farming or ordinary Changi work; that question is left in the explanation rather than converted into a referral of its own."},"discarded_claims":[]}
